This strategy is related to the management of used products from private entities to be sold in second-hand or antique markets via physical or virtual shopping. This commercial system, to be environmental meaningful, should be controlled and analyzed. In this strategy, designers should considerate where the used products come from, the physical condition of the product for potential reselling and timing for cleaning. Usually, second-hand products are sold in different market segments with the lowest price compared to the new one. However in certain segments, second-hand products become increasingly rare, these items can acquire a higher value and be sold with a higher price than a new one.